      "name": "fundamentals coverage assembles a period row from a fact (ADR 0077 T2.1)",
      "_comment": "Coverage is a computed read model returning an object (companyId + periods array), not an array, so the subset harness can only assert its invariant top-level field. expectField is NOT capture-substituted (only step input is), so the companyId is asserted as the deterministic derived id (company_{exchange}_{ticker}, identical on both sides — the same scheme the qualified-ticker journey relies on). Per-cell correctness — a period row with facts.total >= 1 and report null — is pinned by the Rust unit tests and the TS mock scenario tests; this step proves both dispatchers implement the command and key the DTO by the scoped company.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "command": "create_company",
          "input": {
            "input": {
              "exchange": "GPW",
              "ticker": "COVRG",
              "displayName": "Coverage Test S.A.",
